{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>son of elders</b> זקנים is written defective — for he transmitted to him all that he received from the elders, who are Shem and Eber." "<b>son of elders, he is to him</b> ס\"ת אמון — for he transmitted to him סתרי תורה, the secrets of Torah, as it is said of her: ואהיה אצלו אמון ואהיה שעשועים (and I was beside Him as אמון, and I was daily His delight)." "<b>זקנים</b> in gematria equals ר\"ז — for he transmitted to him רזי תורה, the secrets of Torah. And in gematria זר — on account of עטרת זקנים בני בנים (the crown of elders is grandchildren)." "<b>זקנים</b> notarikon: זרעים קדשים נשים ישועות מועד — Seeds, Sanctified, Women, Salvations, Appointed Times." "<b>פסים</b> notarikon: פוטיפר סוחרים ישמעאלים מדינים — Potiphar, Merchants, Ishmaelites, Medanites." "<b>פסים</b> equals in gematria קץ — hinting that through him they descended to Egypt and his sons were enslaved, and the Holy One, blessed be He, subtracted the count of קץ from the bondage. And a hint that he would transmit to him the קץ. And a hint that he would rule פ' years, from the count of סי\"ם, which is the count of his years. Another interpretation: פסים, a term of פסו תמו — for through him he died before his brothers. פסים — that caused reconciliations between him and his brothers. פסים in gematria פס יד לו." "<b>and he made him a ketonet passim</b> in gematria: משקל שני סלעים מילת — the weight of two selas of silk. This is what they said in the first chapter of Shabbat: on account of two selas of silk that Jacob added to Joseph beyond the rest of his brothers, the matter rolled and our fathers descended to Egypt."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {5 "פס יד לו is hyper-literally 'a span of hand to him'; the phrase is obscure and rendered as-is.", 6 "Rendered מילת as 'silk' following the Talmudic context (Shabbat 10b); the word can also mean 'word' but the gematria context and the Talmudic source support 'silk' (מוציא)."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:17:56.602370728Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}